{"step_index":76,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T15:57:12Z","thinking":"**Verifying Syllabus Adjustments**\n\nOkay, so I've confirmed Matplotlib is installed. Now, I'm analyzing the syllabus adjustments. I've successfully identified and removed the \"Tangents and Normals\" and \"Approximations\" sections from the NCERT Class XII Mathematics chapter on applications of derivatives. I also found five questions that touched tang.\n\n\n**Refining Question Replacements**\n\nAlright, I'm now actively planning the replacement questions. For Set A, I've crafted two multiple-choice questions aligning with the revised syllabus focus: one on maximizing a trigonometric function and another on marginal revenue calculation. I've selected these to ensure that the new questions align with the updated topics: rate of change, increasing/decreasing functions, and maxima/minima. Next, I'll continue replacing all other questions.\n\n\n**Calculating Rate of Change**\n\nI've been calculating rates of change and have now addressed additional questions. For Set B, I've worked out solutions and questions that involve the rate of change of volume and surface area, like the cube and sphere problems. I'm focusing on ensuring these examples are clear and representative of the revised syllabus. Additionally, I've begun to strategize the diagram creation.\n\n\n**Generating Visual Aids**\n\nI'm now generating visual aids to support the problems. I have created diagrams for both Set A and Set B. Set A has graphs to illustrate a quadratic function, an equivalence class, and a cost function. Set A also has a velocity-time graph. Set B has diagrams that illustrate the greatest integer function, natural logarithm, a divisibility relation, and a total revenue graph. I will continue generating diagrams as necessary.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Python script to generate high-contrast images for case studies and assertion-reason questions in Set A and Set B.","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"\"\"\"\nGenerate high-contrast diagrams for CBSE Class XII Mathematics Exam 2026-27 (Set A & Set B).\n\"\"\"\n\nimport os\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nimport numpy as np\n\nIMG_DIR = r\"C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\math_exam_2026\\images\"\nos.makedirs(IMG_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n# Set high-contrast style\nplt.rcParams['font.family'] = 'DejaVu Sans'\nplt.rcParams['font.size'] = 11\nplt.rcParams['axes.edgecolor'] = '#000000'\nplt.rcParams['axes.linewidth'] = 1.2\n\n\n# ---------------- SET A DIAGRAMS ----------------\n\ndef gen_set_a_q19():\n    \"\"\"Graph of f(x) = |x - 2|\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    x = np.linspace(-1, 5, 400)\n    y = np.abs(x - 2)\n    ax.plot(x, y, color='#003366', lw=2.5, label=r'$f(x) = |x - 2|$')\n    ax.plot(2, 0, 'ro', markersize=7)\n    ax.annotate('Corner at (2, 0)\\n(Non-differentiable)', xy=(2, 0), xytext=(2.2, 1.2),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=6),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=9)\n    ax.axhline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlabel('x', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('y', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Graph for Q19: Continuity & Differentiability', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.set_ylim(-0.5, 3.5)\n    ax.legend(loc='upper left', framealpha=0.9)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_a_q19.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_a_q20():\n    \"\"\"Graph of f(x) = -(x - 3)^2 + 4\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    x = np.linspace(0.5, 5.5, 400)\n    y = -(x - 3)**2 + 4\n    ax.plot(x, y, color='#006633', lw=2.5, label=r'$f(x) = -(x-3)^2 + 4$')\n    ax.plot(3, 4, 'ro', markersize=7)\n    ax.annotate('Local Maximum (3, 4)\\n$f\\'(3)=0, f\\'\\'(3)<0$', xy=(3, 4), xytext=(1.2, 2.5),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=6),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=9)\n    ax.axhline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlabel('x', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('y', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Graph for Q20: Local Maximum', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.set_ylim(-1, 5)\n    ax.legend(loc='lower center', framealpha=0.9)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_a_q20.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_a_q36():\n    \"\"\"Case Study 1: Equivalence Classes Partition on A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.2, 3.0), dpi=200)\n    \n    # Outer set box\n    rect_main = plt.Rectangle((0.5, 0.5), 9.0, 4.0, fill=False, edgecolor='#000000', lw=2)\n    ax.add_patch(rect_main)\n    ax.text(0.8, 4.1, 'Set A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\n    \n    # Equivalence class [1] = {1, 3, 5} (Odd)\n    ellipse1 = plt.matplotlib.patches.Ellipse((3.0, 2.3), 3.6, 2.4, color='#E6F0FA', ec='#004C99', lw=2)\n    ax.add_patch(ellipse1)\n    ax.text(3.0, 3.1, 'Odd Class [1] = [3] = [5]', ha='center', fontsize=9.5, fontweight='bold', color='#004C99')\n    ax.plot([2.0, 3.0, 4.0], [2.1, 2.4, 2.0], 'o', color='#004C99', markersize=8)\n    ax.text(2.0, 1.7, '1', ha='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\n    ax.text(3.0, 2.0, '3', ha='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\n    ax.text(4.0, 1.6, '5', ha='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\n\n    # Equivalence class [2] = {2, 4} (Even)\n    ellipse2 = plt.matplotlib.patches.Ellipse((7.0, 2.3), 3.0, 2.4, color='#EAF7EA', ec='#006600', lw=2)\n    ax.add_patch(ellipse2)\n    ax.text(7.0, 3.1, 'Even Class [2] = [4]', ha='center', fontsize=9.5, fontweight='bold', color='#006600')\n    ax.plot([6.3, 7.7], [2.1, 2.1], 'o', color='#006600', markersize=8)\n    ax.text(6.3, 1.7, '2', ha='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\n    ax.text(7.7, 1.7, '4', ha='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=11)\n\n    ax.set_xlim(0, 10)\n    ax.set_ylim(0, 5)\n    ax.axis('off')\n    ax.set_title('Figure 1: Equivalence Relation Partition R = {(a,b) : |a-b| is even}', fontsize=10.5, fontweight='bold', pad=4)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_a_q36.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_a_q37():\n    \"\"\"Case Study 2: Total Cost Function Curve C(x)\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.0, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    x = np.linspace(0, 6, 200)\n    # C(x) in thousands for clear scale\n    c = 0.005*x**3 - 0.02*x**2 + 30*x + 5000\n    ax.plot(x, c, color='#B30000', lw=2.5, label=r'Total Cost $C(x)$')\n    \n    # Point at x = 3\n    c_3 = 0.005*(3**3) - 0.02*(3**2) + 30*3 + 5000\n    ax.plot(3, c_3, 'ko', markersize=7)\n    ax.plot([3, 3], [4980, c_3], 'k--', lw=1.2)\n    ax.plot([0, 3], [c_3, c_3], 'k--', lw=1.2)\n    ax.annotate(r'$x = 3, C(3) \\approx ₹5090$', xy=(3, c_3), xytext=(0.8, 5130),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=5),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=9)\n    \n    ax.set_xlabel('Units of Output produced ($x$)', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('Total Cost $C(x)$ in ₹', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Figure 2: Production Cost Curve', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlim(0, 6)\n    ax.set_ylim(4980, 5200)\n    ax.legend(loc='lower right', framealpha=0.9)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_a_q37.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_a_q38():\n    \"\"\"Case Study 3: Velocity-Time Graph v(t) = 3t^2 - 12t + 9\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.0, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    t = np.linspace(0, 3.5, 400)\n    v = 3*t**2 - 12*t + 9\n    ax.plot(t, v, color='#4B0082', lw=2.5, label=r'$v(t) = 3t^2 - 12t + 9$')\n    \n    # Fill area under curve for t in [0, 2]\n    t_fill = np.linspace(0, 2, 200)\n    v_fill = 3*t_fill**2 - 12*t_fill + 9\n    ax.fill_between(t_fill, v_fill, color='#D8BFD8', alpha=0.6, label='Displacement to $t=2$s')\n    \n    # Rest points\n    ax.plot([1, 3], [0, 0], 'ro', markersize=7)\n    ax.annotate('Rest at $t=1$s', xy=(1, 0), xytext=(0.3, 4),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=5),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=8.5)\n    ax.annotate('Rest at $t=3$s', xy=(3, 0), xytext=(2.3, 4),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=5),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=8.5)\n    \n    ax.axhline(0, color='black', lw=1.2)\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', lw=1.2)\n    ax.set_xlabel('Time $t$ (seconds)', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('Velocity $v(t)$ (m/s)', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Figure 3: Velocity vs Time Graph', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlim(-0.2, 3.5)\n    ax.set_ylim(-4, 11)\n    ax.legend(loc='upper right', framealpha=0.9, fontsize=8.5)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_a_q38.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\n# ---------------- SET B DIAGRAMS ----------------\n\ndef gen_set_b_q19():\n    \"\"\"Graph of f(x) = [x] (Greatest Integer Function)\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    for n in range(-2, 4):\n        ax.plot([n, n+1], [n, n], color='#003366', lw=2.5)\n        ax.plot(n, n, 'o', color='#003366', markersize=6)\n        ax.plot(n+1, n, 'o', markerfacecolor='white', markeredgecolor='#003366', markeredgewidth=1.5, markersize=6)\n    \n    ax.axhline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlabel('x', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('y = [x]', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Graph for Q19: Step Discontinuity of [x]', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.set_xlim(-2.5, 4.5)\n    ax.set_ylim(-2.5, 4.5)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_b_q19.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_b_q20():\n    \"\"\"Graph of f(x) = ln(x) for x > 0\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(4.5, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    x = np.linspace(0.1, 5, 300)\n    y = np.log(x)\n    ax.plot(x, y, color='#006633', lw=2.5, label=r'$f(x) = \\ln(x)$')\n    ax.plot(1, 0, 'ro', markersize=6)\n    ax.annotate('(1, 0)', xy=(1, 0), xytext=(1.2, -0.8), fontweight='bold', fontsize=9)\n    ax.annotate(r'$f\\'(x) = \\frac{1}{x} > 0$ (Strictly $\\uparrow$)', xy=(2.5, np.log(2.5)), xytext=(1.8, 0.8),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=5),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=8.5)\n    ax.axhline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', lw=1)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlabel('x', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('y', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Graph for Q20: Monotonicity of log x', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.set_xlim(-0.5, 5)\n    ax.set_ylim(-2.5, 2.0)\n    ax.legend(loc='lower right', framealpha=0.9)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_b_q20.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_b_q36():\n    \"\"\"Case Study 1 (Set B): Divisibility Relation on A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 6}\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.2, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    \n    # Draw nodes\n    pos = {\n        '1': (2.5, 0.6),\n        '2': (1.3, 1.8),\n        '3': (3.7, 1.8),\n        '4': (1.3, 3.0),\n        '6': (3.7, 3.0)\n    }\n    \n    # Draw arrows (a divides b)\n    edges = [\n        ('1', '2'), ('1', '3'), ('1', '4'), ('1', '6'),\n        ('2', '4'), ('2', '6'),\n        ('3', '6')\n    ]\n    \n    for u, v in edges:\n        x1, y1 = pos[u]\n        x2, y2 = pos[v]\n        ax.annotate('', xy=(x2, y2), xytext=(x1, y1),\n                    arrowprops=dict(arrowstyle='->', color='#333333', lw=1.5, shrinkA=12, shrinkB=12))\n    \n    for node, (x, y) in pos.items():\n        circle = plt.Circle((x, y), 0.28, color='#004C99', ec='black', lw=1.5)\n        ax.add_patch(circle)\n        ax.text(x, y, node, color='white', ha='center', va='center', fontweight='bold', fontsize=12)\n\n    ax.set_xlim(0, 5)\n    ax.set_ylim(0, 3.6)\n    ax.axis('off')\n    ax.set_title('Figure 1: Divisibility Relation Graph on A = {1, 2, 3, 4, 6}\\n(Arrow indicates \"divides\")', fontsize=10.5, fontweight='bold', pad=4)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_b_q36.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_b_q37():\n    \"\"\"Case Study 2 (Set B): Total Revenue Function Curve R(x) = 13x^2 + 26x + 15\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.0, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    x = np.linspace(0, 10, 300)\n    r = 13*x**2 + 26*x + 15\n    ax.plot(x, r, color='#CC5500', lw=2.5, label=r'Total Revenue $R(x)$')\n    \n    # Point at x = 7\n    r_7 = 13*(7**2) + 26*7 + 15\n    ax.plot(7, r_7, 'ko', markersize=7)\n    ax.plot([7, 7], [0, r_7], 'k--', lw=1.2)\n    ax.plot([0, 7], [r_7, r_7], 'k--', lw=1.2)\n    ax.annotate(r'$x = 7, R(7) = ₹834$' + '\\n' + r'$MR(7) = ₹208$', xy=(7, r_7), xytext=(2.0, 1000),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=5),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=9)\n    \n    ax.set_xlabel('Units Sold ($x$)', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('Total Revenue $R(x)$ in ₹', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Figure 2: Total Revenue Curve', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlim(0, 10)\n    ax.set_ylim(0, 1600)\n    ax.legend(loc='upper left', framealpha=0.9)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_b_q37.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef gen_set_b_q38():\n    \"\"\"Case Study 3 (Set B): Velocity vs Time Graph v(t) = 6t^2 - 4t\"\"\"\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(5.0, 3.2), dpi=200)\n    t = np.linspace(0, 3.5, 400)\n    v = 6*t**2 - 4*t\n    ax.plot(t, v, color='#006666', lw=2.5, label=r'$v(t) = 6t^2 - 4t$')\n    \n    # Fill area for displacement to t=3\n    t_fill = np.linspace(0, 3, 300)\n    v_fill = 6*t_fill**2 - 4*t_fill\n    ax.fill_between(t_fill, v_fill, color='#B2DFDB', alpha=0.6, label='Displacement to $t=3$s')\n    \n    # Rest point at t = 2/3\n    ax.plot(2/3, 0, 'ro', markersize=7)\n    ax.annotate(r'Rest at $t = \\frac{2}{3}$s', xy=(2/3, 0), xytext=(1.0, -8),\n                arrowprops=dict(facecolor='black', shrink=0.08, width=1, headwidth=5),\n                fontweight='bold', fontsize=9)\n    \n    ax.axhline(0, color='black', lw=1.2)\n    ax.axvline(0, color='black', lw=1.2)\n    ax.set_xlabel('Time $t$ (seconds)', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_ylabel('Velocity $v(t)$ (m/s)', fontweight='bold')\n    ax.set_title('Figure 3: Velocity vs Time Graph', fontsize=11, fontweight='bold', pad=8)\n    ax.grid(True, linestyle='--', alpha=0.5)\n    ax.set_xlim(-0.2, 3.5)\n    ax.set_ylim(-12, 60)\n    ax.legend(loc='upper left', framealpha=0.9, fontsize=8.5)\n    plt.tight_layout()\n    plt.savefig(os.path.join(IMG_DIR, 'set_b_q38.png'))\n    plt.close()\n\n\ndef main():\n    print(\"Generating Set A diagrams...\")\n    gen_set_a_q19()\n    gen_set_a_q20()\n    gen_set_a_q36()\n    gen_set_a_q37()\n    gen_set_a_q38()\n    \n    print(\"Generating Set B diagrams...\")\n    gen_set_b_q19()\n    gen_set_b_q20()\n    gen_set_b_q36()\n    gen_set_b_q37()\n    gen_set_b_q38()\n    \n    print(f\"All diagrams generated in {IMG_DIR}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n","Description":"Script to generate high-contrast diagrams for Set A and Set B case studies and assertion-reason questions.","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\rajan\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\b78a5d36-6586-4c94-a487-70da0c9f5362\\scratch\\generate_diagrams.py","toolAction":"Writing diagram generator script","toolSummary":"Generate diagram script"}}]}
